  Each task defines:
  - description: Human-readable task description
  - commands: Bash commands to execute (required)
  - dependencies: Other tasks that must complete first
  - watch: File patterns to monitor (glob patterns)
  - env: Task-specific environment variables
  - parallel: Run commands in parallel (true/false)
  - continue_on_error: Continue if command fails (true/false)
  - hooks: before/after/on_error lifecycle hooks
  - timeout: Maximum execution time in seconds

EXAMPLES:
  uaft task build                         # Run build task
  uaft task test                          # Run tests (with dependencies)
  uaft task build test --parallel         # Run in parallel
  uaft task dev --watch                   # Watch mode
  uaft task --list                        # List all tasks
  uaft task --info build                  # Show build task details
  uaft task --graph                       # Show dependency graph
  uaft task build --dry-run               # Preview without executing
  uaft task build --debug                 # Verbose logging

EXAMPLE uaft.yaml:
  version: 1.0
  project: my-project

  tasks:
    build:
      description: "Build the project"
      commands:
        - npm install
        - npm run build

    test:
      description: "Run tests"
      dependencies:
        - build
      commands:
        - npm test

    dev:
      description: "Start development"
      watch:
        - src/**/*.ts
      commands:
        - npm run dev

FEATURES:
  • Dependency resolution - Tasks run in correct order
  • File watching - Auto-run tasks on changes
  • Parallel execution - Run independent tasks concurrently
  • Hooks - Pre/post/error callbacks
  • Environment variables - Task-specific configuration
  • TAP output - Machine-readable test format
  • Error handling - Graceful failure and recovery

EXIT CODES:
  0 - All tasks passed
  1 - Task execution failed
  2 - Configuration error
  3 - Circular dependency detected
  4 - Missing dependency task
  5 - Timeout exceeded

TIPS:
  • Use --dry-run to preview before executing
  • Use --watch for development workflows
  • Use --parallel for CI/CD (when safe)
  • Define dependencies to ensure correct execution order

